        "text": "Security update for the Linux Kernel",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "\nThe SUSE Linux Enterprise 16.0 kernel was updated to fix various security issues\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2025-54518: x86/CPU/AMD: Prevent improper isolation of shared resources in Zen2's op cache (bsc#1264013).\n- CVE-2026-46300: net: skbuff: propagate shared-frag marker through pskb_copy() (bsc#1265209).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
